<title>DENMARK: Den Danske Bank to cut staff by 5 pct.</title>
<headline>Den Danske Bank to cut staff by 5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's biggest bank, Den Danske Bank, said on Friday it planned to shed 350 jobs in February with up to 200 more posts cut during the second half of 1997.</p>
<p>A statement said that the present number of 11,100 employees had become excessive in the light of technological advances and was a burden on profit margins.</p>
<p>Negotiations were in progress with staff representatives on compensation and help with re-training and job-seeking, it added.</p>
<p>--Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
</text>
